<header class="mb-6">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-display">Operator</h1>
  <p class="text-foreground/70">
    Every tool that runs the clinic — the rules, the process, the discovery,
    and the helper agent.
  </p>
</header>

<%!-- Each section owns one accent color (chip in the heading, dotted strip
      on its cards, colored lift-shadow on hover). The accents give the hub
      a scavenger-hunt readability: you find the section by its color before
      you read a word. Cards are the shared <.card> recipe; the palette is
      the accent, never the fill — bodies stay white, borders stay black. --%>
<% section_chip =
  "mr-2 inline-block size-3.5 -rotate-6 rounded-base border-2 border-border" %>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-violet"} aria-hidden="true" />Rules &amp; process
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="violet" href="/operator/decisions/appointment.triage/editor">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Decision table editor</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Edit and publish the triage table. A changed rule takes effect on
        the next booking — no deploy.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/operator/processes/appointment_visit/designer">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Process designer</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Draw the visit process: triage, check-in, the consult, labs,
        discharge. Publish a new version of the graph.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/decisions">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Published rules</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Which version of each decision table and process is live, and what
        came before.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/processes">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Published processes</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">The visit process definitions, versioned.</p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="violet" href="/worklist">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Timers &amp; escalations</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Escalation timers ride the tasks themselves — the four-hour lab
        wait shows as a due date here. The engine ships no separate
        trigger UI.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-orange"} aria-hidden="true" />Work
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="orange" href="/operator/tasks">
      <h3 class="font-heading">My tasks</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The engine's own inbox for the acting clinician — claim, complete,
        delegate.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="orange" href="/worklist">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Worklist</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Every open task in one board, completed through the engine so the
        token advances.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="orange" href="/visits">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Visit processes</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Where each visit stands; open one's instance viewer for the token
        overlay on the graph.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<%!-- The Visits surface can't link a row to its instance viewer (the a2ui
     surface DSL has no external row links), so this list is the bridge:
     latest instances, each a link into /operator/instances/:id. --%>
<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-main"} aria-hidden="true" />Recent visit processes
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <%= for instance <- @recent_instances do %>
      <.card accent="main" href={"/operator/instances/#{instance.id}"}>
        <h3 class="font-heading">{instance.subject_label}</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
          Standing at <span class="font-medium">{instance.current_node}</span>
          · status {instance.status}{if instance.outcome, do: " · outcome #{instance.outcome}"}
        </p>
      </.card>
    <% end %>
    <%= if @recent_instances == [] do %>
      <.empty_state icon="hero-heart">
        No visit processes yet — book an appointment and one starts here.
      </.empty_state>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-cyan"} aria-hidden="true" />Discovery &amp; insight
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/canvas">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Data model canvas</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        The whole clinic as a navigable graph — domains, resources,
        relationships — with a surface one click from every node.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/clarity">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Clarity</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Deep introspection: the module graph, ER and policy diagrams,
        supply-chain and security reports. Dev routes only.
      </p>
    </.card>
    <.card accent="cyan" href="/evaluations">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Decision evidence</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Every rule evaluation, with the matched table rows — what the rule
        decided, and why.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-heading">
    <span class={section_chip <> " bg-green"} aria-hidden="true" />Helper agent
  </h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <.card accent="green" href="/agent">
      <h3 class="font-heading">Ask &amp; compose</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/70">
        Ask questions about the clinic's data, or ask for a new interface:
        the agent composes and verifies a surface on the fly and shows it
        beside the conversation. Works without an API key for browsing —
        composing needs one.
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</section>
